    "catalysts": [],
    "industrial_process_notes": "Discovered in 1959 by Allan Hay and commercialized by General Electric in 1960 via oxidative coupling of 2,6-dimethylphenol. Rarely used in pure form due to processing difficulty; General Electric's blended 'Noryl' formulation (PPO/PPE + polystyrene) reached market in the 1960s and remains the dominant commercial form.",
    "synthesis_scheme_image": null
  },
